            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "REA173"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent!! My husband and I loved this dressing. The only change I made was to use 1 tsp. of salt instead of 2 which seemed too much. It was great. Will use this again and again."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AndyM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We've been making this for a couple of years now and never tire of it; it's so good! We call it our \"House Vinaigrette\". But definitely halve the salt! We also bump up the garlic.",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-25T14:17:38.043Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ailina Willis"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow factor! I was in a bind for a vinaigrette and didn't have any balsamic vinegar. This recipe fit my needs. I used olive oil instead of vegetable oil. I halved the salt. I used 1 teaspoon of white sugar and 1.5 teaspoons of honey. Fantastic!",
            "datePublished": "2017-09-04T15:38:02.680Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mike"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe but way too much salt. Try 1/2 tsp as others have suggested.",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-04T21:16:28.640Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Julie Denise Dunk Liberti"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It's a great basic recipe that you can then customize with your own personal tastes. I omitted the sugar &amp; used about 1T. honey &amp; mustard, as well as adding 1 small onion &amp; a few fresh basil leaves &amp; put it all in the food processor! It was SO SO good. I'll be using this for all of my basic vinaigrette recipes &amp; taylor as the mood strikes.",
            "datePublished": "2011-09-23T12:09:47.997Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cincygirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Simple and perfect! I substituted olive oil for the vegetable oil and honey for the white sugar. Mixed in the blender and it was creamy and delicious. I don't think I will buy bottled salad dressing again!",
            "datePublished": "2010-07-12T17:26:22.963Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Paula Sabo Keiper"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent Vinaigrette! The garlic really brings out the flavor. I cut the salt to 1 teaspoon - thought the sodium was too high. Great easy recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-23T10:31:24.480Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DESERTBORN54"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good. I like a vinegar forward vinaigrette. I cut the salt in half. I think next time I'll only cut I by 1/4.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-23T02:43:03.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephanie Fotia Lurito"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I prepared this dressing exactly as it is written. It was WAY too salty. And I am someone who usually likes things a little on the salty side. I would definitely cut the amount of salt in half if I made it again.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-14T12:38:25.987Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Simple and delicious - a really easy and great tasting vinaigrette dressing! I used olive oil vs. vegetable oil and cut the salt down to 1/4 tsp. I also added some cracked black pepper. This was great over mixed greens topped with cucumbers, cherry tomatoes, and thin sliced red onion.",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-20T18:36:14.153Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dfwelf"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love it! I too used less salt but to be fair, I always use less salt the recipe calls for in ANY recipe. I made it without the sugar (I don't like sweet) and it was good as is but then I decided to add a little honey and I admit, it made it better. The vegetable oil is a good idea for a lighter taste. I like it a little heavier. I only had extra virgin olive oil on hand which is too heavy so I did half half veg oil and EVOO. In the end I added a squirt of stone ground mustard, fresh pepper and some dried onion. It was very good either way.",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-26T17:14:38.780Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I don’t expect this to be a hit with many others, but I love red wine vinegar! I used half of the oil (too many calories and I love tart flavors), all the vinegar and nothing else. It is a lot healthier than many dressings, and easy to make (as I have limited mobility). I use light olive oil or canola oil. I’m sure it would be great with vegetable oil too. Edit: I also love it exactly as written. My family prefers this (not surprisingly!) I give the original recipe and my simpler version both 5+ stars!!!",
            "datePublished": "2025-03-01T05:40:59.638Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "John McIlhenny"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I only used 1 tsp of salt and it was amazing. This will be my go to dressing. Highly recommended.",
            "datePublished": "2021-06-27T04:43:40.157Z"
          },
          {
